    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "41ba6e41-f23e-80df-862d-d2ccd84f49e6",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "419a6e41-f23e-8080-aa43-ed67b046bb5f"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-17T04:05:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-17T04:40:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Maybe partly in response to the EAG which first turned me away, maybe inspired by Scott Alexander’s ",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "Maybe partly in response to the EAG which first turned me away, maybe inspired by Scott Alexander’s ",
            "href": null
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "call to open admissions",
              "link": {
                "url": "https://forum.effectivealtruism.org/posts/dsCTSCbfHWxmAr2ZT/open-ea-global"
              }
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "call to open admissions",
            "href": "https://forum.effectivealtruism.org/posts/dsCTSCbfHWxmAr2ZT/open-ea-global"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": ", I’ve had the policy of never running admissions for Manifest. Anyone is allowed to purchase a ticket and attend. And surprisingly, this seems to have worked okay!",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": ", I’ve had the policy of never running admissions for Manifest. Anyone is allowed to purchase a ticket and attend. And surprisingly, this seems to have worked okay!",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "41ba6e41-f23e-80ac-b910-f6ec88ec642c",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "419a6e41-f23e-8080-aa43-ed67b046bb5f"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-17T04:09:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-17T04:41:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Manifest operates off of positive selection: highlighting specific speakers and topics which show what Manifest should be about, coupled with almost unreasonable amounts of cold outreach and discretionary tickets sent to people who I think would make the experience good. And in the beginning, the nicheness of “prediction markets” ensured that only the nerds would turn out. “Prediction markets” have now exploded, but Manifest has built up a culture of its own. It might help that we don’t advertise too much; that word-of-mouth remains the primary way by which people consider attending each year.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "Manifest operates off of positive selection: highlighting specific speakers and topics which show what Manifest should be about, coupled with almost unreasonable amounts of cold outreach and discretionary tickets sent to people who I think would make the experience good. And in the beginning, the nicheness of “prediction markets” ensured that only the nerds would turn out. “Prediction markets” have now exploded, but Manifest has built up a culture of its own. It might help that we don’t advertise too much; that word-of-mouth remains the primary way by which people consider attending each year.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "41ba6e41-f23e-80ad-9649-f3fa1c2d3d11",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "419a6e41-f23e-8080-aa43-ed67b046bb5f"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-17T04:17:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-17T04:46:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "To be determined if this gateless ideal will hold up — the latest incarnation of Manifest pushed Lighthaven to its limits, almost bursting at the seams — but I hope that it will, or that we will be clever enough to find good workarounds. Perhaps we shard attendees throughout days; perhaps we host parts in a park. (In many ways, the free & open-to-public Night Market is the Manifestiest part of Manifest.)",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "To be determined if this gateless ideal will hold up — the latest incarnation of Manifest pushed Lighthaven to its limits, almost bursting at the seams — but I hope that it will, or that we will be clever enough to find good workarounds. Perhaps we shard attendees throughout days; perhaps we host parts in a park. (In many ways, the free & open-to-public Night Market is the Manifestiest part of Manifest.)",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "41ba6e41-f23e-80f6-9113-f1cddb86a5c4",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "419a6e41-f23e-8080-aa43-ed67b046bb5f"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-17T04:42:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-17T04:46:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "How far can this extend? I recently wrote about how ",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "How far can this extend? I recently wrote about how ",
            "href": null
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "AI may allow for more porous org boundaries",
              "link": {
                "url": "https://austin.site/posts/fluid-org-boundaries-with-ai"
              }
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "AI may allow for more porous org boundaries",
            "href": "https://austin.site/posts/fluid-org-boundaries-with-ai"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": ". And though AI cometh, we may not need AI for orgs, movements, and states which operate with open borders; just the will to try.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": ". And though AI cometh, we may not need AI for orgs, movements, and states which operate with open borders; just the will to try.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
